        Root cause:
        The bug originates from using an invalid guest DMA address saved in the guest's GGTT table without prior validation or pinning, which can lead to DMA faults and GPU hangs when the address is accessed by the host thread. This oversight can occur due to the asynchronous nature of updates by the vCPU thread and subsequent usage by the qemu UI thread.

        Commit message:
        drm/i915/gvt: Pin vgpu dma address before using

Dma-buf display uses the vgpu dma address saved in the guest part GGTT
table which is updated by vCPU thread. In host side, when the dma
address is used by qemu ui thread, gvt-g must make sure the dma address
is validated before letting it go to the HW. Invalid guest dma address
will easily cause DMA fault and make GPU hang.

